{"title":"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/c/19ce43eacb173b610f4104e4efa33eca16e1c213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC,\\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"45\" height=\"16\" /> angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is a right angle and the altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/1/181fc7e4fc45bb8783db936cb7e663284b47b062.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C\\,$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" /> meets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/d/6cde21d43fca31ff965c25786ef0a718644be777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}\\,$\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/790afaf99abb61bd5b921bbf5e703fa95f49e0bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D.\\,$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />  The lengths of the sides of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/7/bd750bbb25ede334c0796583ce94891b33c097cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC\\,$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> are integers, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/b/0db3dfa2516afa1a76def49230872fc1acb63d5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD=29^3,\\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/c/2dcd43e4f9f746333ef0e4274222dc0478911257.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos B=m/n\\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/b/70bf49cca6e1987b33f7a3b2da51a3c56527455a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\,$\" width=\"15\" height=\"8\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/9/349097a0033d438020f14d96381b189edc30c186.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\,$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" /> are relatively prime positive integers.  Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/4/994bb8f7d1cabda58067818e3b26160f6f5c1bec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n.\\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/6/946a0fe64b74572c32927f5c1a381940be3e3a40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC \\sim \\triangle CBD$\" width=\"143\" height=\"13\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/a/14a50faa0c51c82a9335b8abff2a67471c4009ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{BC}{AB} = \\frac{29^3}{BC} \\Longrightarrow BC^2 = 29^3 AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"243\" height=\"39\" />. It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/2/eb2704c2ece3e43305b4e79b9ffbe2c474858ddb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$29^2 | BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/2/be2f7b95f5a25b68d562e6aed5cee17090b2c714.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$29 | AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> are in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/d/1cd84dc4a06ebcc334e6d874b308b1d042b7524c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$29^2 x$\" width=\"35\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/a/21aee59befcc1595cb0bc7b08049af10e031d49c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$29 x^2$\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" />, respectively, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer. \n</p><p>By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a>, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/9/7893aa20845d4b380f363dc68ade20b564a84fac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC^2 + BC^2 = AB^2 \\Longrightarrow (29^2x)^2 + AC^2 = (29 x^2)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"389\" height=\"19\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/8/d88961eae013d9e2711e87bb3871a82ff9e39312.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$29x | AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />. Letting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/b/b3b52b82093631fac9ff2a87b641c5016c209f2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = AC / 29x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"18\" />, we obtain after dividing through by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/4/bf4e572d28e7c600024f3ba7e2052e0377302e7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(29x)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"48\" height=\"19\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/f/03f3e7e7b5da79acc9bf1dc31b1362cb8c35fc15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$29^2 = x^2 - y^2 = (x-y)(x+y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"242\" height=\"19\" />. As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/1/40128b12f7092e3906531e930c41c5f7235912f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y \\in \\mathbb{Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"15\" />, the pairs of factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/8/bd81b0717e30a5e25ea6bd7c76751d4cc27a9a79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$29^2$\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/6/586c5af09c4ac6fedd66b618d272be8086a1198d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,29^2)(29,29)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"114\" height=\"19\" />; clearly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/4/be41d8b2075aaf5e8955e8ae9922ce45e9265d6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\frac{AC}{29x} \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"99\" height=\"38\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/4/3e434d8c85b206f764b152bb48e18dc348c38d13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-y = 1, x+y= 29^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"174\" height=\"18\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/c/c9cc87721c82ff2930142b7eb1065c92d7a25933.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{1+29^2}{2} = 421$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"146\" height=\"39\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/8/0a8bb51d1f0b4143bedb79fef85ac36a4d8ae111.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos B = \\frac{BC}{AB} = \\frac{29^2 x}{29x^2} = \\frac{29}{421}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"217\" height=\"39\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/8/c98bc84e2a1d36022f21ae1d24cd72c3e4b5dbfe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n = \\boxed{450}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We will solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/c/1dc0f84230d6166da3a17d8ebfdb5d0178da2c49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos B$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" /> using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/6/86644a0d74ba9ba18fc2e69713901863ab6c3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CBD$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />, which gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/5/50591ca36b9d02be6bfc4e01e44a9a469cc3e334.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos B = \\frac{29^3}{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"97\" height=\"39\" />. By the Pythagorean Theorem on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/6/86644a0d74ba9ba18fc2e69713901863ab6c3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CBD$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/e/6fec54f0a82c0cf608919dd676b50021aa7861fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC^2 - DC^2 = (BC + DC)(BC - DC) = 29^6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"359\" height=\"19\" />. Trying out factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/b/ceb6f6c9e1f4fe47ffa4c83ee29824e2e8b6bd43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$29^6$\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" />, we can either guess and check or just guess to find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/c/55cbd6c7e29eb1ef83da4757107924eb4605aaa0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC + DC = 29^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"130\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/2/ba28b669d25755dc29fe8f0e3fb6f93ae3b36a24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC - DC = 29^2$\" width=\"129\" height=\"15\" /> (The other pairs give answers over 999). Adding these, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/c/c5cb0ab9c1b816ee8d1fcff4a49cc822acea9748.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2BC = 29^4 + 29^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"134\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/7/5b7114e0eabdd91a434f40c3c4a57aff8334c9fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{29^3}{BC} = \\frac{2*29^3}{29^2 (29^2 +1)} = \\frac{58}{842} = \\frac{29}{421}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"267\" height=\"43\" />, and our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/a/8eab674e2460fabeea03a5623f7d18b7fc43fec2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{450}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using similar right triangles, we identify that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/1/221bde02c1b0781a3c3b326bffff48a0783cf272.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD = \\sqrt{AD \\cdot BD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"142\" height=\"18\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/c/5ac4e76c31f8776f4a7b814ba18a59fa6703f603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$29 \\cdot k^2$\" width=\"47\" height=\"15\" />, to avoid too many radicals, getting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/e/7de9ac9917ec0fb7d5a2dead253d391017518cb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD = k \\cdot 29^2$\" width=\"101\" height=\"15\" />. Next we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/f/01f72b330b8d166e55e3ccc4f2c601f6e0a04553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = \\sqrt{AB \\cdot AD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"138\" height=\"18\" /> and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/6/766806d04df0743cf3a0add6e2141ef57b7ecdf8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = \\sqrt{AB \\cdot BD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"140\" height=\"18\" />. Applying the logic with the established values of k, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/0/1b0c53ddc48ca7074637a341e45eaeae92270634.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = 29k \\cdot \\sqrt{29^2 + k^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"174\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/2/fd298ae0fad314b7ae8b6ba2a2ad2b5f53aaf787.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 29^2 \\cdot \\sqrt{29^2 + k^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"172\" height=\"18\" />. Next we look to the integer requirement. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is both outside and inside square roots, we know it must be an integer to keep all sides as integers. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1d3d4bef88dd7d7478feef08e9b90d24d72baf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{29^2 + k^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" />, thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/a/e1a0a3fb87775879929228bcf55bd92a66e8f7ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$29^2 = y^2 - k^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"105\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/c/32cc34c1b1704cfa5f809a0b66552f2f9ad05ba8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$29^2 = (y + k)(y - k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"160\" height=\"19\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/5/0657f5cd42256c0a39d45b265235e2a939625515.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$29$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> is prime, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> cannot be zero, we find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/a/2cac29923301388793a23f2aa010bce5dd581b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 420$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/f/1ffbb8594021dd3bc5903f91c43e4f58d235bd51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 421$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" /> as the smallest integers satisfying this quadratic Diophantine equation. Then, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/0/c605ad7c1d0d89071939d2e6992e40ec4413e600.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$cos B$\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/d/66d1aca3d85aa810d5e5f45c9941f14ac43d7468.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{29}{\\sqrt{29^2 + k^2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"82\" height=\"42\" />. Plugging in we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/3/003d4f58564668ea1bc3b9c11a9d99fef18552d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$cos B = \\frac{29}{421}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"93\" height=\"38\" />, thus our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/a/8eab674e2460fabeea03a5623f7d18b7fc43fec2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{450}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME\" title=\"1994 AIME\">1994 AIME </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1994 AIME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=1994\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1994_AIME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1994 AIME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<